        "props": [
          {
            "_comment": "Mass is 2.0 kg, not a round 5.0. The box is 0.2 x 0.15 x 0.1 m, so 0.003 cubic metres, and 5 kg of it is 1667 kg per cubic metre, denser than packed sand. 2 kg is 667, a heavily packed carton, and it leaves headroom under the UR5e's 5 kg rating for a 196 mm tool that hangs the box its full height below the flange. The GPU run of 2026-09-16 carried 5 kg and the wrist visibly swung, stalling j3 6 to 10 degrees short of every place waypoint. Measured, not derived. pick-station reports `corner at (200, -1200, 220)` in its own get_attributes summary, and its box_origin_offset_mm is (200, 900), so the infeed origin is (400, -300). Its frame-declared collider spans x 200..600 and y -1200..-100, which contains that point. z is the station top at 220 plus half a 100 mm box. An earlier calculation read the offset against the station's FRAME instead of its corner and got (600, 250), which is 350 mm past the near edge, so the box fell to the floor. The other seven boxes are parked clear of the cell at x -2000, an invented spot that only has to be out of the way, and the palletizer re-poses each onto wherever box_props[0] actually rests.",
            "name": "infeed_box_1",
            "type": "cube",
            "size": 0.05,
            "scale": [
              4.0,
              3.0,
              2.0
            ],
            "position": [
